let __v_4887 = Value::from("Fresh water boiled once, one teabag per mug, three to four minutes and then the bag out: that is the whole of a good cup, and the milk goes in last. Green tea wants cooler water, about 80C, for two to three minutes, and black tea wants it just off the boil, three to five. Bitter tea has steeped too long in water that was too hot, and a mug that tastes of the last one is a bag left sitting in it.");
frame.store("TEA_METHOD_TEXT", __v_4887.clone())?;
let __v_4888 = Value::from("Warm the pot first with a splash of boiling water swirled round and tipped away, then one teabag or one teaspoon of leaves per cup and one extra for the pot, water just off the boil, three to four minutes. Take the bags or leaves out before it goes to the table, and a cosy keeps the second cup hot without stewing it.");
frame.store("TEA_POT_TEXT", __v_4888.clone())?;
let __v_4889 = Value::from("Cold brew it: eight teabags to a litre of cold water in the fridge overnight, bags out in the morning, then lemon and sugar to taste, which has none of the bitterness of a hot brew cooled down. In a hurry, brew double strength in a mug of boiling water for four minutes, take the bags out, and pour it over a jug of ice.");
frame.store("TEA_ICED_TEXT", __v_4889.clone())?;
let __v_4890 = Value::from("Cloudy tea is the minerals in hard water binding with the tannin, and it is harmless to drink: filter the water, or use bottled, to get it clear, or add a small pinch of bicarbonate of soda to the pot, which keeps the tannin dissolved. It is not a dirty kettle and it is not a sign the tea has gone off.");
frame.store("TEA_CLOUDY_TEXT", __v_4890.clone())?;
let __v_4891 = Value::from("Green tea wants water at about 80C for 2 to 3 minutes; black tea wants it just off the boil for 3 to 5. Bitter tea is nearly always tea that steeped too long in water that was too hot, and sour or stewed tea is a pot left standing on a warmer or in the leaves: pour it off them and make the next one weaker and shorter.");
frame.store("TEA_FAULT_TEXT", __v_4891.clone())?;
let __v_4892 = Value::from("Green tea wants water at about 80C rather than boiling, for two to three minutes: boil the kettle and let it stand for a minute or two, or add a splash of cold water first. Water straight off the boil makes it bitter, and green tea goes bitter quickly, so pull the bag out at three minutes and drink it soon after.");
frame.store("TEA_GREEN_TEXT", __v_4892.clone())?;
let __v_4893 = Value::from("A second cup from the same teabag is weak and mostly colour, but it is harmless: if you want it stronger, use a fresh bag and pull it out sooner instead. Reuse one within the same hour at most, and not once it has been sitting in milk.");
frame.store("TEA_TWICE_TEXT", __v_4893.clone())?;
