let __v_5142 = Value::from("Lay a sheet of foil loosely over the top as soon as it starts to colour, and turn the oven down 10 to 20C (or move the tin a shelf lower): a cake that catches on top is nearly always an oven running hot, a shelf too high or a dark tin, not the mixture. If the top is brown and the middle still wobbles, cover it and give it another 10 to 15 minutes rather than turning the heat up. If the bottom is already black, cut that off, trim the dark top and serve the rest - and next time check your oven with a thermometer, since most run 10 to 20C hotter than the dial says.");
frame.store("_BAKE_PREVENTION", __v_5142.clone())?;
let __v_5143 = Value::from("Cut or grate the black off once it has cooled, and if only the top is dark the rest is fine - a dark top on a fruit cake is often just the sugar. If the middle is still wet, cover the tin loosely with foil and give it another 10 to 15 minutes. Next time move the oven shelf down one and tent the tin with foil after 20 minutes, because a bake burns on top while the middle is still wet.");
frame.store("_BAKE_BURNT", __v_5143.clone())?;
