let __v_5151 = Value::from("Lift the shelf up one, slide a baking sheet or two under the tin to take the direct heat and drop the oven 10C, because a bottom that burns first means too much heat from underneath and a hot oven burns the base while the middle is still wet. Line a dark or thin tin with baking paper, and turn the tin if one corner of the oven browns hard. If the top is browning before the middle is set, lay a sheet of foil loosely over it so the base can catch up. If the bottom has already caught, cut or grate the black off and eat the rest, and check the oven once with a thermometer, since most run 10 to 20C hotter than the dial says.");
