let __v_6104 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"jacket potato\",\"jacket potatoes\",\"baked potato\",\"baked potatoes\",\"potato skins\"]},\"A jacket potato is fine the next day: cool it within an hour, keep it in the fridge covered and eat it within 2 days, skin and all. Reheat it until it is piping hot right through, or cut it up and fry it - a foil-wrapped one left on the side overnight goes in the bin.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"coleslaw\",\"slaw\"]},\"Coleslaw keeps 3 days in the fridge once it is opened, and homemade 2, because it is the mayonnaise that turns. Keep the tub cold and eat it by the date on it, and bin slaw that smells sharp or has gone watery in the bottom of the tub.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"scone\",\"scones\",\"fruit scone\",\"cheese scone\"]},\"Scones are best the day they are made and keep 2 days in a tin, or a day in the fridge. Sprinkle them with water and give them 3 minutes in a warm oven to bring them back; freeze them on the day and refresh from frozen, and bin any with green on them.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sushi\",\"shop sushi\",\"sushi box\"]},\"Shop sushi is made to be eaten the day you buy it: keep it in the fridge, eat it within 24 hours and do not leave it out on the side. The rice and the raw fish are what go off, so bin what is left rather than keeping it for tomorrow.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tuna\",\"tinned tuna\",\"tin of tuna\",\"canned tuna\"]},\"An opened tin of tuna keeps 2 days in the fridge, emptied into a bowl with a lid - left in the tin it tastes of metal. Eat it cold in a sandwich or flake it through a sauce, and do not freeze it, because it comes back dry and woolly.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cooked salmon\",\"cooked fish\",\"leftover salmon\",\"leftover fish\",\"smoked salmon\"]},\"Cooked salmon keeps 2 days in the fridge, covered, and it is better cold in a salad than reheated, which dries it out. Cool it within an hour of cooking and bin it after 2 days; smoked salmon keeps 3 days once the pack is open and freezes for a month.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"prawn\",\"prawns\",\"cooked prawns\",\"king prawns\"]},\"Cooked prawns keep 2 days in the fridge, in a sealed box away from anything raw, and ones from the deli counter keep a day less than a sealed pack. Eat them cold or warm them through in a sauce rather than frying them again, and bin any that smell of ammonia.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"gravy\",\"gravies\",\"onion gravy\",\"leftover gravy\",\"brandy sauce\"]},\"Gravy keeps 2 days in the fridge, less than the meat does, because it is mostly liquid and it cools slowly in the jug: get it in within 2 hours of making it, standing the jug in a bowl of cold water if it is still hot. Reheat it until it boils right through, and bin any that has sat out on the table all evening.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"stuffing\",\"sage and onion\",\"forcemeat\",\"stuffing balls\"]},\"Cooked stuffing keeps 2 days in the fridge and it is the leftover to be strict with, because it has been inside the bird and soaked up the juices: cool it within 2 hours, box it, and reheat it until it is piping hot right through. Stuffing that never went in the oven is a different thing and keeps as long as the bread in it.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"custard\",\"homemade custard\",\"custard sauce\",\"creme anglaise\"]},\"Homemade custard keeps 2 days in the fridge, in a jug with a lid or a sheet of cling film pressed onto the surface so no skin forms. Reheat it gently and stir rather than boiling it, and bin any that has stood on the table through dinner.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"trifle\",\"trifles\",\"sherry trifle\"]},\"A trifle keeps 2 days in the fridge, and it is the cream and the fruit that turn rather than the sponge: cover it once it is made and eat it within a day or two. Do not freeze it - the cream splits and the sponge goes watery.\"]}]}")?;
