let __v_6174 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"egg\",\"Eggs going spare: a frittata or a tortilla takes six or eight at once with whatever veg is in the fridge, a quiche takes four plus milk and cheese, and meringues or a pavlova use up whites on their own. Hard boiled, they keep a week and make sandwiches, or halve them into a salad with mustard and oil.\"],[\"chicken\",\"Cooked chicken: shred it into a salad with mayonnaise, lemon and something crunchy, or stir it through fried rice with soy sauce and peas for a 10-minute dinner.\"],[\"potato\",\"Leftover potatoes: crush them a little and fry them in hot oil until crisp, or slice them into a frittata with eggs.\"],[\"pasta\",\"Leftover pasta: loosen it in a hot pan with a splash of water and a little oil, or bake it with a spoon of tomato sauce and cheese on top.\"],[\"salmon\",\"Leftover salmon: flake it through pasta or a salad with lemon and yoghurt, and don't reheat it hard or it dries out.\"],[\"bread\",\"Stale bread: tear it into croutons fried in oil and garlic, or blitz it into breadcrumbs and freeze them.\"],[\"lentil\",\"Leftover dhal: thin it with a splash of stock into soup, or eat it cold as a dip with bread and yoghurt.\"],[\"coconut milk\",\"Half a tin of coconut milk: simmer it with curry paste and whatever veg you have for 10 minutes, or stir it into rice instead of water for a coconut rice. It freezes in an ice cube tray for next time.\"],[\"cream\",\"Cream or soured cream going spare: stir it into a chilli or curry off the heat so it does not split, spoon it over baked potatoes or fruit, or let it down with a squeeze of lemon and use it as a dressing. Soured cream also freezes badly, so use it rather than keep it.\"],[\"sprout\",\"Leftover sprouts: halve them and fry cut side down in butter until they caramelise, about 8 minutes, or shred them raw into a salad with lemon, oil and toasted nuts.\"],[\"marrow\",\"Half a marrow left: scoop out the seeds, stuff it with mince and rice and bake it 45 minutes at 190C (170C fan), or grate it into a curry - the water it gives up thickens the sauce as it cooks.\"],[\"buttermilk\",\"Buttermilk going spare: soda bread takes 284ml, or thin a pancake batter with it, or marinate chicken in it for an hour before frying - it tenderises the meat.\"],[\"hot cross bun\",\"Buns going stale: butter them and bake them in a bread and butter pudding, or halve and toast them under a grill with a little sugar on top.\"],[\"stuffing\",\"Leftover stuffing: shape it into balls and fry or roast them 15 minutes at 200C (180C fan), or press it into a tray and cut it into crisp squares - it is the best part of the tray, so do not bin it.\"],[\"porridge\",\"Leftover porridge: loosen it with milk and reheat it, or beat in an egg and fry spoonfuls in butter for oat fritters with jam.\"],[\"bolognese\",\"Leftover bolognese: bake it with pasta and white sauce, spoon it over a jacket potato, or thin it with stock and beans into a soup.\"],[\"curry\",\"Leftover curry: reheat it once until piping hot and eat it with rice, or bake it under a mash topping for a curry pie.\"]]}")?;
